### Voice and Interface

| What it does | Claude | Gemini | ChatGPT | Copilot |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Talk to your Agent by voice | Voice (mobile) | Voice (mobile) | Voice / Advanced Voice | Voice |
| Mobile app | iOS / Android | iOS / Android | iOS / Android | iOS / Android |
| Desktop app | Mac / Windows | (browser) | Mac / Windows | (built into Windows) |
| Browser integration | (extension) | Chrome integration | (extension) | Edge built-in |

---

### Paid vs. Free

| | Claude | Gemini | ChatGPT | Copilot |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Free tier name | Claude (free) | Gemini | ChatGPT Free | Copilot (free) |
| Standard paid tier | Claude Pro | Google AI Pro | ChatGPT Plus | Microsoft 365 Premium |
| Standard paid price | ~$20/mo | ~$20/mo | $20/mo | ~$20/mo |
| Higher paid tiers exist | Yes (Max) | Yes (Ultra) | Yes (Pro) | Enterprise |
| Key paid benefit | Higher limits, extended thinking, Projects | Latest Gemini model, more Gems | Full access to flagship model, more GPTs, ability to create custom GPTs | Priority access, bundled with Office apps and storage |

_Microsoft retired the standalone Copilot Pro plan in late 2025 and folded its AI features into Microsoft 365 Premium, which bundles them with the Office apps and extra storage rather than selling AI access on its own._

_All pricing and feature availability subject to change. See [majordomo.dwk.io/features](https://majordomo.dwk.io/features) for current information._

---

### The One That Matters Most for This Book

*Projects (Claude) = Gems (Gemini) = Custom GPTs (ChatGPT)*

If you read one section of this table, read this one. The most powerful technique in this book — building a persistent context for a domain of your life so your AI majordomo already knows your situation — requires this feature. The names differ. The capability is the same. Once you have set up a Project, Gem, or custom GPT for your household, your health situation, or your finances, every subsequent conversation in that space starts with your majordomo already briefed. On ChatGPT's free tier, build the same thing with Custom Instructions plus Memory instead — creating a new custom GPT requires Plus.

The book's Chapter 3 explains how to use this. This table tells you what to look for in your tool of choice.
